.TH "CSSMATHINVERT" "3JS" "August 7, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSMathInvert \- CSSMathInvert
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathInvert\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents the inverse (reciprocal) of a
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathInvert()\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathInvert.value\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object containing the value being
inverted.
.SH STATIC METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
When you divide one \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] by another using
\f[CR]div()\f[R], if the divisor is a plain number, it can immediately
be scaled into a value of the original type.
.PP
If the divisor is a different type, the result can\(cqt be resolved to a
single object.
In this case, the CSS Typed Object Model API represents the divisor as a
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R].
.PP
Generally you won\(cqt construct a \f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] directly.
It\(cqs produced when \f[CR]div()\f[R] is called with a divisor that
isn\(cqt a plain number: the result is a \f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R], and
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] is the operand holding that divisor \(em found
by walking the product\(cqs operands, or by checking
\f[CR]CSSMathValue.operator\f[R] for the string
\f[CR]\(dqinvert\(dq\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] serializes using CSS \f[CR]calc()\f[R] syntax,
as \f[CR]calc(1 / <value>)\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Constructing a CSSMathInvert with a non\-number divisor
This example shows how you can use \f[CR]div()\f[R] with a divisor that
isn\(cqt a plain number to get a \f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R] that has a
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] as one of its operands.
The value and serialization of that operand are also logged.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] product = CSS.px(200).div(CSS.percent(4));

console.log(product.constructor.name); \f[I]// \(dqCSSMathProduct\(dq\f[R]
console.log(product.values[1].constructor.name); \f[I]// \(dqCSSMathInvert\(dq\f[R]
console.log(product.values[1].value); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 4, unit: \(dqpercent\(dq}\f[R]
console.log(product.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqcalc(200px / 4%)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
